{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: make the worker timeout test independent of whether the child has emitted a diagnostic before cancellation. This is a small test-only child of ordinary-filing test correction #22533 (3a4a54e4), assigning the additional path/outcome before it joins that work. Keep the S1 correction and its review/landing ahead of both; full Tailapp I7 and other existing commitments remain intact. You may deliver the two test outcomes together on request/filing-progress-test in one worktree and one independently reviewed head, with both commitments explicitly accounted for in its artifact/review/landing plan.\n\nYour finding 899be0c4 reports one failure of TestWorkerProcessRetainsTimeout under load during the oversized merge-tree gate: the worker was killed, but stderr was empty. Subsequent isolated runs passed. I independently inspected [the timeout fixture and assertion](cmd/gitseq-perf/worker_process_test.go@c0108be875f08345d1ac83bde94019b6aadc7082:64) and [the timeout/capture path](cmd/gitseq-perf/main.go@c0108be875f08345d1ac83bde94019b6aadc7082:502), and verified both files are byte-identical at current main c0108be875f08345d1ac83bde94019b6aadc7082, the worker landing1a5f1586 and approved af599ecf. I have not reproduced the load-dependent failure myself.\n\nThe fixture already writes its message before exec sleep30. Moving that print before the sleep therefore does not repair the reported race: the timeout can expire before the child reaches its first write or even starts. Preserve proof of timeout enforcement without requiring an unobserved emission. Keep the independent neighboring success/process-error/decode-error tests that prove diagnostic capture, wrapped error handling, strict JSON and result validation. Do not weaken timeout testing to accepting any unrelated error.\n\nAdd the smallest deterministic control for cancellation without a prior diagnostic and preserve a control that fails when the worker timeout is removed. Account for the legitimate before-start context-deadline path as well as a started process being killed. Use a bounded fixture that does not leave sleeping children holding pipes. No repeated machine-load campaign, broad timing-only test harness, production timeout or output-capture change is commissioned. The goal is faithful timeout and diagnostic coverage without relying on process startup timing.\n\nScope is cmd/gitseq-perf/worker_process_test.go and directly necessary test-only support. The parent continues to own cmd/gs/event_reference_test.go; the queued typed Git-output production fix #22459 (dc4890cf) remains separate. If sharing the parent worktree, state that choice before editing and preserve both named conditions in the final reporting artifact and guarded review/merge plan. Follow independent exact-head Architecture/Security/Simplification review, requester ratification, sealed exact-path succession, source/sequence/receipt push, CI and owned worktree/local/remote-branch cleanup. Same-outcome review corrections stay on this child’s live commitment; no resident operations are assigned.","body":{"branch":"request/filing-progress-test","conditions":"Test-only additional outcome to22533: worker timeout enforcement remains proven when no child diagnostic was emitted, including pre-start cancellation; preserve independent stderr/error/strict-result controls and a timeout-removal control. No production behavior change or load campaign. May share parent worktree/head with explicit two-commitment artifact/review/sealed closure accounting; push, CI and owned cleanup. S1 and existing queue first.","head":"c0108be875f08345d1ac83bde94019b6aadc7082","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2fe11f1e769cf8a256f35f5c154c4f6e18db9cb9, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:3a4a54e46766c73f8ce6220b949303cf9816bba2, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:899be0c41313ea31208bee7479a503a6dfb2cc2c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b